# Module Federation Conventions

- Remote apps expose modules; the dashboard consumes them via the `remotes` map in
  `apps/dashboard/vite.config.ts`. When adding a new exposed module or remote entry,
  update both the exposing app's federation config and the dashboard's `remotes` map.
- `react` and `react-dom` are shared as singletons across federation boundaries — do
  not introduce a second copy or a conflicting version range in any app's
  `shared` config without checking every other app.
- Federated modules load from `http://localhost:<port>/remoteEntry.js` in dev. Don't
  hardcode these URLs outside vite config; keep ports consistent with the table in
  `README.md`:
  - dashboard (host): 5173
  - prompt-manager: 5174
  - guardrail: 5175
  - user-manager: 5176
  - usages-data: 5177
- **Dual mode:** every remote must work as a standalone Vite app on its port and as a
  federated remote in the dashboard. CSS strategy (per-remote pipeline + host content scan):
  1. Each remote owns `tailwind.config.ts` (preset from `@repo/ui`), `postcss.config.js`,
     `src/index.css` (`@tailwind` layers), and imports `@repo/ui/tokens.css` + `./index.css`
     from `src/main.tsx` (standalone entry only — not from the federated `./App` expose).
  2. Standalone `index.html` uses `class="dark"` (SPEC default) and loads Inter + JetBrains Mono.
  3. Dashboard `tailwind.config.ts` `content` also scans that remote's `src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` so
     federated mounts get utility classes from the host stylesheet without a second global CSS
     inject from the remote. Wired for prompt-manager (#108), guardrail (#109), and
     user-manager (#110); remaining remote tracked in #111.
- Be cautious with global/shared state across federation boundaries — each remote is
  a separately bundled app and can't assume in-memory state from another remote.
- When scaffolding a new remote app, mirror the existing `vite.config.ts` federation
  block (name, exposes, shared react/react-dom singletons), wire it into the
  dashboard's `remotes` map, and include the same Tailwind / `@repo/ui` CSS entrypoints
  as sibling remotes before considering the app "integrated."
